body:
Based on the data from the gist I could create a minimal reproduction scenario for Elasticsearch 5.4.1 consisting of only one document (attached compressed as [geometry.json.zip](https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/files/1180167/geometry.json.zip)).

```
curl -XDELETE "http://localhost:9200/speedlimit"

curl -XPUT "http://localhost:9200/speedlimit" -d '
{
  "mappings": {
    "speedlimit": {
      "properties": {
        "geometry": {
          "type": "geo_shape",
          "tree": "quadtree",
          "precision": "100m"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}'
# ensure that you've unzipped geometry.json.zip from the attachment above
curl -XPOST 'http://localhost:9200/_bulk?pretty' --data-binary @geometry.json
```

Will lead to:

```
{
  "took" : 33813,
  "errors" : true,
  "items" : [
    {
      "index" : {
        "_index" : "speedlimit",
        "_type" : "speedlimit",
        "_id" : "AV2EWf3T4RDVowrFsHtQ",
        "status" : 400,
        "error" : {
          "type" : "mapper_parsing_exception",
          "reason" : "failed to parse [geometry]",
          "caused_by" : {
            "type" : "array_index_out_of_bounds_exception",
            "reason" : "-1"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

and in the logs:

```
